From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: x <x@x>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 23:30:00 +1100
Subject: [PATCH] 0153: blueline GPU: user interface (BlueGPU, msm ABI for
 mesa-ios/bluedrm)

Stage 6d of pixel3-ios-gpu/gpu-stage6-plan.md, on top of 0147 and 0151.
Kernel side of the GPU user interface; the ABI is mesa-ios/blue_gpu_uapi.h
(copied byte for byte to iokit/Kernel/arm/blue_gpu_uapi.h; userland owns
it): Linux drm/msm, selector = DRM_COMMAND_BASE + DRM_MSM_* (GEM_CLOSE
0x09, USERPTR 0x7d, IOSURFACE 0x7e as HakiOS), the struct in and back
through IOConnectCallStructMethod, mmap = IOConnectMapMemory64 with the
GEM handle as the memory type.

New files (most of the patch):
 - bsd/dev/blueline_gpu_mem.c: the GPU pool, a physical carve-out below
   4 GiB that XNU does not manage (default 32 MiB at 0xc0000000, at most 32 MiB (ml_io_map region),
   bluegpu_pool_mb / bluegpu_pool_base; refused outside 0xa4000000..
   0xe0000000 or if any page is managed RAM), kernel view write-combined,
   64 KiB first-fit. GPU VA, one table for everything (per-process tables
   are stage 2): L1[2] 0x80000000 = the pool, linear, 2M blocks; L1[3]
   0xc0000000 = imports, 4K PTEs. The pool's first 4 MiB hold the tables.
 - iokit/Kernel/arm/BlueGPUUserClient.cpp: the IOService "BlueGPU" (on
   IOResources, published by the bring-up thread once resident) and
   BlueGPUUserClient: GET/SET_PARAM, GEM_NEW, GEM_INFO, CPU_PREP/FINI,
   SUBMIT, WAIT_FENCE, GEM_CLOSE, MADVISE, SUBMITQUEUE_*, USERPTR,
   IOSURFACE. Struct sizes exact, handles per connection, IBs only from
   the caller's own pool BOs and inside them, no relocs, fences checked
   against what was issued. Closed BOs wait for their fence and for the
   last task mapping. IOSurfaces: one handle per surface per connection,
   clean to PoC at submit (seed or 4 ms), invalidate at CPU_PREP.
   bluegpu_uapi_test=1: an in-kernel client through the same operations
   (CP_MEM_WRITE + 2D fill IB, ring wrap, CPU_PREP, busy close, refusals,
   userptr) logging "BLUEGPU TEST:" lines.
 - bsd/dev/blueline_gpu_core.h: the C interface between the three.

bsd/dev/blueline_gpu.c, one block marked 0153 before rs_cpu plus four
small hunks: the ring is shared, so every ring write holds
blue_gpu_ring_lock and checks space against RPTR (presents too; a present
is never queued behind user work, it is a CPU copy then); rs_recover
(0151's, renamed rs_recover_unlocked) runs under the lock and retires
every user fence; rs_irq wakes user waiters; the bring-up thread calls
blue_gpu_uapi_start(). User submit: CCU/cache invalidate, WFI,
CP_ALWAYS_ON, CP_INDIRECT_BUFFER per IB, WFI, CP_ALWAYS_ON, the present
path's 2D state again, CCU flush TS x2, CACHE_FLUSH_TS, WFI, CP_MEM_WRITE
seq (target page +0xa00), CACHE_FLUSH_TS | IRQ.

Boot-args: bluegpu=8 (needed), bluegpu_uapi=0 (off), bluegpu_pool_mb,
bluegpu_pool_base, bluegpu_uapi_hang_ms (1000), bluegpu_uapi_test=1.
Not tested on the phone yet (draft).

The design follows HakiOS's msm-DRM clone (drivers/gpu/hakios.gpu.cpp,
APSL 2.0) and ios-flame 0113 (MIT); no code copied.
---
